# Licensed font binaries.
#
# `frontend/public/fonts/*.woff2` was ignored here until 2026-08-20, and the two
# Satoshi files are now COMMITTED instead. The rule was not wrong, it was
# load-bearing in the wrong direction: every Dokploy build starts from a git
# checkout, so ignoring the binaries shipped a production image with no fonts.
# `/fonts/Satoshi-Variable.woff2` 404'd, the SPA fallback answered index.html,
# and the browser reported `OTS parsing error: invalid sfntVersion: 1008821359`
# — 0x3C21646F, the ASCII for `<!do`. Satoshi is load-bearing (DNA §3) and the
# self-hosted @font-face in proovd.css is the required setup, so the font has to
# be in the image.
#
# This rests on THIS REPOSITORY BEING PRIVATE. Self-hosting Satoshi is what the
# Fontshare licence is for; publishing the binaries is redistribution and is
# not. If this repo is ever made public, the files come out again and reach the
# image another way (a build-time fetch from R2 is the shape that was costed).
#
# docs/fonts/ holds spare statics and stays out — nothing builds from it.
docs/fonts/
# Same rule for the fonts shipped inside a supplied design reference: the bundle
# is kept on disk so the prototype runs standalone, but the binaries are not ours
# to redistribute. Delete the folder and re-copy from the bundle if it goes missing.
docs/design-refrence/**/fonts/
